<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  What the app's FileProvider is allowed to hand out content:// URIs for.

  This shipped as Capacitor boilerplate granting <external-path path="."/> —
  the root of shared external storage, i.e. every photo, download and document
  on the device — plus <cache-path path="."/>. Nothing in this app ever asked
  for either. The provider is exported="false", so a URI still has to be handed
  out deliberately, but a path that broad turns any future mis-issued grant
  into a read of the user's whole SD card rather than of one file.

  The only real consumer is Capacitor core: BridgeWebChromeClient photographs
  into getExternalFilesDir(DIRECTORY_PICTURES) when a WebView <input type="file">
  offers the camera, then wraps it with getUriForFile against this provider.
  That is an external-files-path (app-private, no shared storage), and it is
  the one entry kept. Removing it entirely would leave that path throwing
  IllegalArgumentException instead of failing gracefully.

  The task document itself is not here on purpose: import and export go through
  the Storage Access Framework, where the user picks the file and the URI comes
  from the system picker, so tasks.json never needs a grant of its own.
-->
<paths xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <external-files-path name="captured_images" path="Pictures" />
</paths>
